From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:30:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] media: cec: add Samsung SDP (Nike-L) Micom HDMI-CEC
 interface

Build 070 (CEC, P1): Linux 6.6 port of linux-4.1.10/drivers/soc/sdp/
sdp_micom_cecif.c (Dongseok Lee, Samsung, GPL) from Samsung's GPL package
20_DTV_NikeL, in its cec-framework variant
(CONFIG_SDP_MICOM_CECIF_SUPPORT_SUBSYSTEM). The controller in the Micom
block ("samsung,sdp-mc-cecif") is shared with the Micom; the driver keeps
the bit timing the Micom programmed and refuses to enable while the Micom
still owns it.

Changes: kfifo, timer_setup(), IRQF_NO_AUTOEN, physical address 0.0.0.0
(TV). Not ported yet: the Micom firmware version check (needs the
samsung,sdp-micom-ctrl driver), debugfs.

DT: mccmu syscon and cec nodes from the firmware DT (status disabled).
Compile-only: nothing was run on a TV.
---
